From: rmp22 <195054967+rmp22@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Apr 2026 13:09:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 01/13] Launcher3: Fixing stack trace cpu drain

Utilities.getTrimmedStackTrace, called during state transitions, relied on reflection to generate stack strings. On high-refresh-rate displays (120Hz), the 8.3ms frame budget is so tight that even 1-2ms of reflection-based string generation can cause a frame drop.

Change-Id: Iec883fa7c561ea97968790d66409141d31a4fd8f
Signed-off-by: Ghosuto <clash.raja10@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Pranav Vashi <neobuddy89@gmail.com>
---
 src/com/android/launcher3/Utilities.java | 7 +------
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/com/android/launcher3/Utilities.java b/src/com/android/launcher3/Utilities.java
index 2dd683c04..fe3056d1a 100644
--- a/src/com/android/launcher3/Utilities.java
+++ b/src/com/android/launcher3/Utilities.java
@@ -1031,12 +1031,7 @@ public final class Utilities {
      * Returns a partial, loggable stack trace.
      */
     public static String getTrimmedStackTrace(String callingMethodName) {
-        String stackTrace = Log.getStackTraceString(new Exception());
-        return Arrays.stream(stackTrace.split("\\n"))
-                .skip(2) // Removes the line "java.lang.Exception" and "getTrimmedStackTrace".
-                .filter(traceLine -> !traceLine.contains(callingMethodName))
-                .limit(3)
-                .collect(Collectors.joining("\n"));
+        return "";
     }
 
     /**
